        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;Key design decisions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;• Postgres owns correctness (system of record); OpenSearch owns read performance (derived index)&lt;br&gt;• The index is never the system of record, so rebuilds and mapping changes carry no data risk&lt;br&gt;• Inference and enrichment run at ingest, never on the serving path&lt;br&gt;• Attribution assertion signed Ed25519, single-use, 1-hour expiry&lt;br&gt;• Commission rate embedded in the signed assertion (neither side can alter it)&lt;br&gt;• PHP for application layer, Go for latency-sensitive data path (ADR-0001)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F9FAFB;strokeColor=#D1D5DB;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="800" width="620" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="scalenote" value="&lt;b&gt;OpenSearch ingest discipline (implemented in ingest-svc)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;• Bulk API, refresh_interval -1 during load, replicas 0 then restored&lt;br&gt;• async translog durability during load, force merge on completion&lt;br&gt;• Zero-downtime rebuild via atomic alias swap (products → products_vN)&lt;br&gt;• At platform scale: read replicas serve the API, primary absorbs ingest writes;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;connection pools isolated per workload; vector quantization above ~100M vectors&lt;br&gt;• See docs/SCALING.md&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF7ED;strokeColor=#FDBA74;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="800" width="570" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

